<td width="100%" valign="top" align="left" class="aligned-bullets" style="text-align: left; font-family: Chivo, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: #223341; font-size: 16px; font-weight: normal; letter-spacing: normal; line-height: 24px; padding-bottom: 40px; width: 100%;"> <p style="margin: 0px;">‌<br /></p> <p style="margin: 0px;">The<a style="color: #223341;" href="https://flywire.foleon.com/report/income-collection-benchmarking-2024/?utm_source=marketo&amp;utm_medium=email&amp;utm_campaign=q3clientnewsletter"><span style="color: #48b985;"><strong> <u>report</u></strong></span></a> offers a comprehensive view of the policies and strategies employed by UK universities to manage financial risk, mitigate debt, and enhance international student retention.</p> <p style="margin: 0px;">‌<br /></p> <p style="margin: 0px;">Research findings reveal some more subtle themes among institutions with lower default and bad debt rates which tend to have:</p> <p style="margin: 0px;">‌<br /></p> 
<ul style="margin-bottom: 0px !important; margin-top: 0px !important;"> 
<li>Higher deposit rates</li> 
<li>More flexibility with instalment plans</li> 
<li>Effective sanctions in the event of non-payment</li> 
